                         ┌──────────────┐
                         │    Answer    │
                         └──────────────┘
                                 ▲
                                 │
                    ┌──────────────────────────┐
                    │         Memory           │
                    │  Conversation history    │
                    │  (always active)         │
                    └──────────────────────────┘





Component	       Description	                                                        Location

User	              External actor who submits the query to the agent.	              N/A

**invoke_agent**     Entry point. Orchestrates the full agent flow.                        `src/agent/agent.py` → `invoke_agent()` |
**Semantic Router**  Embedding-based router that decides which tool to use.                `src/agent/agent.py` → `_semantic_decisions()` |
**Tool Execution**   Executes the selected tools and collects their results.               `src/agent/agent.py` (inside `invoke_agent`) |

**RAG Tool**         Searches internal PDF documents.                                      `src/agent/tools.py` → `search_documents()` |
**API Tool**         Queries the local FastAPI server for machine data.                    `src/agent/tools.py` → `get_machine_api_status()` |

**Vector Store**     FAISS index + chunk metadata.                                         `src/rag/vector_store.py` → `search_vector_store()` |
**API Server**       FastAPI REST API for machine data.                                    `src/server/main.py` → `get_machine()` |


**LLM**              Generates the final answer from tool results and context.             `src/agent/agent.py` → `llm.invoke()` |
**Memory**           Stores conversation history for follow-ups.                           `src/agent/memory.py` → `ConversationMemory` |


**PDF Loader**       Loads PDFs, cleans text and splits them into chunks.                  `src/rag/pdf_loader.py` → `load_pdf()` / `create_chunks()` |
**Embedding Model**  Multilingual model shared by the Semantic Router, the RAG Tool and the PDF Loader. | `src/config.py` → `EMBEDDING_MODEL` · used in `src/agent/agent.py` and `src/rag/embeddings.py` |

Answer	              Final output generated by the LLM and returned to the user.	              N/A (output)




# 🛠️ TECH STACK 

Layer	       Technology	                            What it really tells you

LLM	       llama3.2:3b via Ollama	              Small 3B local model via Ollama. No cloud APIs. Fast but less powerful than GPT-4.
Embeddings	paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2 
              (SentenceTransformers)	              Multilingual, lightweight embedding model used via SentenceTransformers. Supports ES/EN/DE/IT/FR. This is the Embedding Model.
Vector Store	FAISS (IndexFlatIP, cosine similarity)	FAISS with exact inner-product search and cosine similarity. Precise for small/medium sets, not optimized for scale.
RAG	       pypdf + custom chunking with overlap	PDFs read with pypdf. Custom overlapping chunking with text cleaning. Source + page metadata preserved.
API	       FastAPI + Uvicorn	                     REST API server for machine data, served with Uvicorn.
HTTP          Client	requests	                     API Tool uses requests to call the FastAPI server.
Agent	       Custom semantic router + LangChain Ollama	No full agent framework. Custom semantic router plus LangChain only for Ollama/LLM integration.
Testing	pytest	                                   18 automated tests with pytest.
Language	Python 3.13	                            Entire project in Python 3.13. Very recent, possible library compatibility issues.




## 📁 Project Structure

llm-ai-agent/
│
├── documents/                    # Stores the PDF files that the RAG will index
├── vector_store/                 # Holds the FAISS index and chunk metadata
│
├── tests/                        # Verifies that the agent, router and tools work
│   ├── test_memory.py            # Checks that memory stores and recalls context
│   ├── test_router.py            # Checks that the router selects the correct tools
│   └── test_tools.py             # Checks that the RAG and API tools return data
│
├── src/                          # Contains the full source code of the project
│   ├── config.py                 # Centralizes all parameters (LLM, API, router, memory)
│   ├── main.py                   # Starts the interactive chat loop with the agent
│   │
│   ├── agent/                    # Implements the reasoning layer of the agent
│   │   ├── agent.py              # Routes questions and executes the selected tools
│   │   ├── tools.py              # Exposes RAG and API as callable tools
│   │   ├── memory.py             # Stores and retrieves conversation history
│   │   └── prompts.py            # Defines the system prompt and behaviour rules
│   │
│   ├── api/                      # Handles communication with the REST API
│   │   ├── client.py             # Sends HTTP requests to the FastAPI server
│   │   └── services.py           # Wraps API endpoints into reusable functions
│   │
│   ├── rag/                      # Implements the Retrieval-Augmented Generation pipeline
│   │   ├── pdf_loader.py         # Loads PDFs and splits them into chunks with metadata
│   │   ├── embeddings.py         # Converts text chunks into normalized embeddings
│   │   ├── vector_store.py       # Builds, saves, loads and searches the FAISS index
│   │   └── rag_pipeline.py       # Retrieves the most relevant chunks for a question
│   │
│   └── server/                   # Exposes a local REST API
│       └── main.py               # Serves machine data through FastAPI endpoints
│
├── pytest.ini                    # Configures pytest for the test suite
├── requirements.txt              # Lists the Python dependencies of the project
└── README.md                     # Documents the project for users and reviewers



## 🚀 INSTALLATION  

1. Clone the repository

       git clone https://github.com/pedrotenza/llm-ai-agent.git
       cd llm-ai-agent

2. Create and activate a virtual environment

       python -m venv venv
       venv\Scripts\activate        # Windows
       # source venv/bin/activate   # Linux/macOS

3. Install dependencies

       pip install -r requirements.txt

4. Install and pull the LLM

       ollama pull llama3.2:3b

5. Add PDF documents

       Place your PDF files in the documents/ folder.

6. Build the vector store

       python -m src.rag.vector_store

7. Start the API server (in a separate terminal)

       python -m uvicorn src.server.main:app --reload

8. Run the agent

        python -m src.main




## 🔄 DAILY WORKFLOW  


# Navigate to the project
cd G:\software-projects\llm-applications\llm-ai-agent

# Running the system (two terminals)


Terminal 1 — API server:


venv\Scripts\activate                           # Activate the virtual environment
python -m uvicorn src.server.main:app --reload


Terminal 2 — Agent:

venv\Scripts\activate                            # Activate the virtual environment
python -m src.main


# (Optional) Update requirements if you installed new packages
pip freeze > requirements.txt

⚠️ The API server must be running before you start the agent, otherwise the API tool will fail.



